      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bendigo’s historic tram sheds, built in 1903, now house a museum that preserves the city’s once‑extensive tram network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bendigo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bendigo Joss House, constructed by Chinese miners in the 1860s, is the only surviving temple of its kind in regional Victoria.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bendigo",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Surrounding Bendigo, the Box‑Ironbark forest of the Greater Bendigo National Park supports swift parrots and other woodland birds, a key feature of the local ecosystem.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
